        "ecology": "Exposed reed margins and grass embankments provide food, perches, laying ground and open travel. The fictional Longwing follows plant and shelter conditions between connected patches. Sheet metal provides a perch or shadow, not nutrition. Dense resting groups can be conspicuous to a catcher, but group membership does not certify pedigree, high output or a compatible reproductive pair. Earlier references to “exposed grass” are expanded into these two local populations without establishing a new continent or a fixed planetary climate.",
