        "anatomy": "A supported lever arrangement for the forewings and fan hindwings, retaining each surface group’s permitted travel and the required return path. Folding joints and beat-transmission joints have different functions even where they share a root region.",
        "measurement": "Working travel, resistance, repeatable return and fold clearance, with flight output assessed as a complete installed system. Force/travel choices are ranges rather than universal higher grades.",
        "fitting": "Choose the lever range and ground/fold clearances with the host and support bridle present. A fixed pattern supplies an ordinary stroke. Dynamic adjustment requires included actuation.",
