        "handling": "Unloaded root supports, protected stops and a clear folded/open diagram. Structural folding wear and living interface readiness remain separate inspection points.",
        "buyer": "Longline makers and owners changing between sustained travel and more responsive approaches.",
        "boundary": "The return motion is part of the working cycle; it is not free recovery energy that can be spent again as propulsion."
      },
      {
        "id": "W18.PREP.BRIDLE",
        "name": "Flight-root bridle / support arrangement",
        "role": "Frame function and load path",
        "source_refs": [
          "W14.PART.BOXBRACE",
