        "anatomy": "Latch, compliant thoracic hinge, specified loading arrangement and supported roots. The package declares whether it includes loading tissue or uses a compatible host-driven path.",
        "measurement": "Seating, input work, useful release motion, permitted body flex and return readiness at a stated burden. A maximum snap is not a guarantee of an upright result.",
        "fitting": "Position for the actual host/support relationship and preserve the bending region. Link to available supply and controller where needed; fit a different support shape rather than clipping through a stiff brace.",
        "working_sequence": "Seat, load, release, make actual contact and recover running. It can be used again only after real readiness and resources permit. It cannot restore a lost race gate.",
